Apple today released iOS 27.0.1, the first update for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> update that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/apple-releases-ios-27/">came out two weeks ago</a>. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Face-ID-iPhone-18-Pro.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066479" /><br/>
iOS 27.0.1 can be downloaded over the air by going to Settings > General > Software Update. Apple has also released iPadOS 27.0.1 and visionOS 27.0.1 updates, as well as iOS and iPadOS 26.7.1 updates for devices not updated to iOS and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a>.<br/>
<br/>
According to Apple's release notes, iOS 27.0.1 addresses an issue that could cause <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> not to work properly on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Some <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/iphone-18-pro-face-id-issues/">iPhone 18 Pro users have complained</a> that authentication can fail to work for things like unlocking a locked app. In some cases, the device freezes up and then reboots. Other users have seen a "&zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; is Not Available" message when attempting &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; setup, and others have experienced issues with the Require Attention for &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; setting. Apple's release notes for the update are below.<br/>
<blockquote>This update provides bug fixes for your iPhone, including fixes for the following issues:<br/>
<br/>
- iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max may unexpectedly restart when Face ID fails to authenticate<br/>
- A color artifact may appear on photos captured at 2x under certain lighting conditions at f/1.48 on a small number of iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max devices<br/>
- Opening Notification Center and Control Center simultaneously may cause the touchscreen to become unresponsive</blockquote><br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models have an infrared camera that's under the display for the first time, but it's unclear if the hardware has been causing a problem. Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/24/ios-27-update-face-id-issue-iphone-18-pro/">said last week</a> that it would be able to address the &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; bugs with a software update.<br/>
<br/>
